1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,882
Most strategies don't fail on bad logic.

2
00:00:02,882 --> 00:00:06,176
They fail on one assumption nobody was paid

3
00:00:06,176 --> 00:00:07,000
to attack.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,517
That's red team coaching.

5
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:11,552
Not a sixty-page deck — coaching your team

6
00:00:11,552 --> 00:00:14,586
to think like the competitor, the regulator, and

7
00:00:14,586 --> 00:00:17,621
the angry customer, before reality does it for

8
00:00:17,621 --> 00:00:18,000
you.

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,097
The cheapest place to find a fatal flaw

10
00:00:21,097 --> 00:00:22,645
is on the whiteboard.

11
00:00:22,645 --> 00:00:25,355
The most expensive is after the launch.

12
00:00:25,355 --> 00:00:28,452
A premortem flips it: it's eighteen months out,

13
00:00:28,452 --> 00:00:30,000
this failed — why?

14
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,097
In one session a team surfaces the assumption

15
00:00:33,097 --> 00:00:36,194
they agreed with too fast, stress-tests the plan,

16
00:00:36,194 --> 00:00:38,516
and leaves with owned, dated actions.

17
00:00:38,516 --> 00:00:41,613
Decision quality as a capability — installed, not

18
00:00:41,613 --> 00:00:42,000
rented.

19
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,267
What's the last big decision your team made

20
00:00:46,267 --> 00:00:50,000
that nobody was asked to argue against?
